      "summary": "The router sends supported missing-requirement claims to review and creates no request. However, the extra claim-text containment check can suppress review for claims that meet the clarification’s stated structural checks.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/ClaimValidator.cs",
          "line": 70,
          "message": "The claim-text check adds a structural requirement the clarification does not specify. A valid requirement identifier can appear in the witness and typed value while the claim describes that requirement by name; this check downgrades the claim and prevents internal review.",
          "confidence": 0.95,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "After validating the current witness, digest, and typed value in the quote, Validate also requires the typed value to appear verbatim in claim.Text. A failure downgrades the claim, which FindingRouter sends to NoAction.",
            "failureScenario": "A structurally valid claim says “Reserve approval is missing,” its typed requirement identifier is “R-42,” and the current witness quote contains “R-42 pending.” Because the claim text does not contain “R-42,” validation downgrades it and routing creates nothing, instead of sending the structurally valid MissingRequirement claim to internal review as the issue requires."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
